# Konsultasi & Kontrol Rp0 — "Selesai Tanpa Biaya" (rule 217)

**Status:** deployed 2026-11-01, runtime `4520a276` (GO tag
`feature-rme-rp0-control-consultation-1-implementation-go`), production-verified, flag **OFF**.

Sprint record: `docs/sprints/feature-rme-rp0-control-consultation-1.md`. Owner decision package and
answers: `docs/decisions/rme-rp0-control-consultation-owner-decision-package.md`; register entry
"S6-D1 … S6-D8" in `docs/decisions/rme-billing-correction-owner-decisions.md`. Cashier SOP (Indonesian):
`docs/operations/rme-rp0-selesai-tanpa-biaya-sop.md`. ADR: `docs/adr/0014-rme-zero-value-closure.md`.

## 1. What it is

Before this rule a Rp0 invoice was created `UNPAID` and could never be paid (a payment needs
`amount > 0`), so a Rp0 Konsultasi on a new visit stayed `cashier_pending` forever and a Rp0 Kontrol only
completed when the patient happened to pay an UNRELATED receivable in the same batch (production
invoice #36). "Selesai Tanpa Biaya" is the explicit way out.

- **`NO_CHARGE`** ("Tanpa Biaya") is a terminal invoice status. It is **not** `PAID`: no payment row,
  no receipt, no lab candidate, no revenue. It is **not** a receivable: not `UNPAID`/`PARTIAL`.
- Written ONLY by `RmePaymentService::closeZeroValueInvoice()`, through
  `RmeInvoiceRepositoryInterface::closeAsNoCharge()`. The provenance columns
  (`zero_value_category`, `zero_value_closed_by`, `zero_value_closed_at`) are not fillable and are bound
  to the status by three PostgreSQL CHECKs (`NO_CHARGE` ⇔ provenance set; `NO_CHARGE` ⇒ `grand_total = 0`;
  category vocabulary).

## 2. Eligibility (S6-D1, S6-D6) — `RmeZeroValueEligibility`, the single answer

Evaluated on the LOCKED invoice and visit. Refusal codes are stable; branch on the code.

1. Invoice `UNPAID` (`ZERO_VALUE_INVOICE_NOT_OPEN`); total exactly Rp0 (`ZERO_VALUE_TOTAL_NOT_ZERO`);
   `correction_version = 0` (`ZERO_VALUE_INVOICE_CORRECTED`); no payment row ever, soft-deleted included
   (`ZERO_VALUE_HAS_PAYMENTS`); visit `cashier_pending` (`ZERO_VALUE_VISIT_NOT_PENDING`); at least one line.
2. **Every line genuinely free:** `unit_price = 0` AND `discount = 0` (`ZERO_VALUE_LINE_NOT_FREE`). A Rp0
   reached by discount is a discount, not a free service — D21c stays PENDING.
3. **Never the voucher** `TRT-FREESC`, on any visit, Kontrol included (`ZERO_VALUE_VOUCHER_EXCLUDED`).
4. **Kontrol** = `visit_type = control` AND `follow_up_of_visit_id` set (server-derived, never a client
   field): ~~every free line is eligible (owner sub-decision)~~ — **SUPERSEDED 2026-11-01 by S6-Q3
   (revised), see §9:** on a Kontrol only an approved free service may be Rp0. **Any other visit:** every line must be a
   treatment in a consultation category (`consultation`); a free-text line or another treatment is
   refused (`ZERO_VALUE_CATEGORY_NOT_ELIGIBLE`). Eligibility comes from `treatment_id` + category,
   never from a description.
5. The lists are source-controlled in `config/rme_zero_value_closure.php` with NO environment read.
   Widening them is a reviewed code change that needs a new owner decision.
6. **Narrowed after the independent security review** — originally recorded as pending owner
   confirmation; **both APPROVED by the Owner on 2026-11-01 as S6-Q1 and S6-Q2 (§9)**:
   - a Kontrol must follow a REAL examined visit of the same patient: the parent exists, is not
     soft-deleted, and is `cashier_pending` or `completed` (`ZERO_VALUE_CONTROL_PARENT_INVALID`). A link
     to a cancelled or never-examined visit is a label, not a follow-up;
   - a line whose treatment `requires_lab` is never closed free (`ZERO_VALUE_LAB_LINE_EXCLUDED`):
     `NO_CHARGE` generates no lab candidate, so closing it would silently drop the lab work.
   Relaxing either needs a new owner decision.

## 3. The transaction (S6-D2, S6-D3, S6-D7)

- Lives beside `pay()` on purpose: it takes the SAME invoice row lock first and inherits the SAME
  cashier guards by construction — active RME branch, usable persisted account, `manage_rme_billing`,
  working branch (`assertCashierMayCollect`), the D10 correction hold and the rule 203 dispute hold
  (`assertNoPaymentHold`). Then the visit row is locked and eligibility is decided.
- One transaction: invoice → `NO_CHARGE`, visit → `completed` (`ClinicVisitService::transitionStatus`),
  one audit row `RME_INVOICE_ZERO_VALUE_CLOSED`. The row SNAPSHOTS the eligibility inputs (per line:
  treatment id/code, category code, `requires_lab`, unit price, discount; plus `visit_type`,
  `follow_up_of_visit_id`, parent status, `payment_count = 0`), because master data can be edited after
  the closure. Codes and ids only — a free-text line description is never copied (it may name a patient).
- Every refusal, including the inherited guards, answers under the ONE key `zero_value`, which the
  cashier page always renders (`data-zero-value-error`). A refusal is never silent.
- **Idempotent:** an already-closed invoice is answered as it stands (no second transition, no second
  audit row), and only to an account that still has the authority.
- **Super Admin's `Gate::before` never reaches eligibility** — a business rule, not a permission.
- The invoice branch is the visit branch; a request never names a branch, amount, category or status.
  `CloseRmeZeroValueInvoiceRequest` carries only the cashier's acknowledgment.
- No new permission: the HTTP door is `RmeInvoicePolicy::closeZeroValue` (same scope as `pay`), route
  `rme.cashier.zero-value-closure.store` inside the `permission:manage_rme_billing` group.

## 4. Financial invariants (each pinned by a test)

`RP0_DOES_NOT_CREATE_FAKE_PAYMENT` · `RP0_DOES_NOT_INCREASE_REVENUE` · `RP0_DOES_NOT_CREATE_FALSE_RECEIVABLE`
· `RP0_DOES_NOT_ERASE_REAL_RECEIVABLE` (a Kontrol closure never touches the parent's receivable — OD-1a)
· `RP0_DOES_NOT_WRITE_REFUND` / `PATIENT_CREDIT` · `RP0_DOES_NOT_BYPASS_BILLING_DISPUTE` ·
`RP0_DOES_NOT_BYPASS_D28` · `RP0_DOES_NOT_BYPASS_DISCOUNT_POLICY` · `RP0_DOES_NOT_MODIFY_HISTORICAL_INVOICES`
· `RP0_IS_NOT_PAID`. Never record a payment, receipt or refund to stand in for a closure, and never set a
`NO_CHARGE` invoice back to `UNPAID` by hand.

## 5. D28 and neighbours (S6-D4)

D28 (rule 201) is unchanged: a Rp0-original invoice is never corrected, and a `NO_CHARGE` invoice is not
`UNPAID` either. Disputes refuse `NO_CHARGE` (`BILLING_DISPUTE_INVOICE_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED`); payments,
refunds and lab-candidate generation never see it. Rp0 ISSUANCE is unchanged (D21g for issuance stays
PENDING).

## 6. Reporting (S6-D5)

A closed Rp0 visit is a clinical visit with zero revenue: Owner KPI `rp0_visits` / `rp0_consultations` /
`rp0_controls` (period on `zero_value_closed_at`, branch-filtered); never in revenue, receivables,
"belum dibayar" counts or "Lunas"; doctor performance adds `no_charge_item_count` ("Item Tanpa Biaya").
Every invoice status label map renders `NO_CHARGE` as "Tanpa Biaya". The oversight room-treatment view
keeps a closed Rp0 treatment on the day it was performed (`BILLED_INVOICE_STATUSES` includes `NO_CHARGE`).
`config/dq1.php` accepts the status, and DQ1-DATA-004 counts a `NO_CHARGE` invoice that carries ANY
payment row (soft-deleted included) as an anomaly — the "no payment row" invariant has no table-level
CHECK because it spans two tables.

## 7. Flag (S6-D8)

`rme.zero_value_closure` default **OFF** (`FEATURE_RME_ZERO_VALUE_CLOSURE`, captured at config build,
rule 92). While off: the route and its FormRequest answer 404, the service refuses
(`ZERO_VALUE_NOT_ENABLED`), and every CASHIER page renders exactly as before. The read-only reporting
additions (Owner KPI "Kunjungan Tanpa Biaya" card, doctor-performance "Item Tanpa Biaya" column and filter
option) render regardless of the flag; they read 0 until a closure exists and have no financial effect.

With the flag on, only an ELIGIBLE Rp0 invoice trades "Bayar" for "Selesai Tanpa Biaya". An ineligible
Rp0 invoice keeps its payment entry (a Kontrol's carry-over collection starts there), so no visit is left
stranded at `cashier_pending`. The handoff marker only says "buka untuk cek" — it never promises
eligibility. Turning it on in production
is `ACTIVATION-RME-RP0-CONTROL-CONSULTATION-1`: a separate Owner decision after verification and the SOP.
Rollback = flag off; closed invoices stay closed.

## 8. Residuals (recorded, not decided)

- **Operator-controlled inputs (security review MEDIUM-1) — NARROWED 2026-11-01 by S6-Q3 (§9), NOT closed;
  severity unchanged (MEDIUM, not release-blocking under S6-D3/D21).** The named vector — a Kontrol link making a
  normally paid treatment free — is closed by code and tests. What remains (independent hardening review): the
  cashier still chooses each line's treatment under D21 and nothing reconciles it with the medical record or
  odontogram, so a performed paid procedure can still be billed as "Konsultasi Dokter" Rp0 (or left off); and what is
  free depends on master-data category (`manage_clinic_master_data`, in practice Super Admin). Control: detective
  only — the oversight "Tanpa Biaya (Rp0)" breakdown and self-issued count. ~~Recommended follow-up (not built): an
  oversight cross-check of NO_CHARGE visits whose clinical record shows a procedure.~~ **BUILT 2026-11-01 as rule
  218** (`HARDENING-RME-RP0-CLINICAL-BILLING-CONSISTENCY-1`, owner CB-Q1/Q2/Q3): a DETECTIVE clinical vs billing
  cross-check recorded with every closure and shown in oversight; a signal never refuses (a fault fails closed). MEDIUM-1 is now
  `PARTIALLY_MITIGATED` (rule 218 §8), still not closed. Historical text: Under D21 the unit price is typed by the
  cashier, and the Kontrol link is chosen at registration, so one branch account can still bill a
  non-consultation treatment at Rp0 on a Kontrol and close it. Rule §2.6 removes the cancelled and
  never-examined parent; the rest is policy, not code. Mitigations available to the Owner, none decided:
  a per-cashier NO_CHARGE drilldown (the audit row already records `zero_value_closed_by` and the line
  snapshot), a time window on the parent visit, or creator ≠ closer (S6-D3 chose no second approval).
- **Irreversible by design.** `NO_CHARGE` is terminal; correction, refund and dispute refuse it and there
  is no void. A mistaken closure has no in-app undo — this is why the cashier must acknowledge it.

**RESOLVED 2026-11-01 for every closable invoice (§9.4).** Historical text: The existing Kontrol batch path (`completeControlVisitIfSettled`) can still complete a Rp0 Kontrol visit
when the patient pays an unrelated parent receivable from the Kontrol cashier page; that invoice then
stays `UNPAID` (the #36 pattern) and is no longer closable (visit not pending). With the flag on, the
cashier page offers the closure INSTEAD of the payment button for an eligible Rp0 invoice, and tells the
cashier to collect the parent receivable from its own invoice. Changing the batch path itself needs an
owner decision.

## 9. HARDENING 2026-11-01 — owner S6-Q1, S6-Q2, S6-Q3 (revised) (`HARDENING-RME-RP0-CLOSURE-OWNER-DECISIONS-AND-PAID-TREATMENT-1`)

Sprint record: `docs/sprints/hardening-rme-rp0-closure-owner-decisions-and-paid-treatment-1.md`. Register:
"S6-Q1 … S6-Q3b" in `docs/decisions/rme-billing-correction-owner-decisions.md`. Where this section and
§2–§8 disagree, **this section wins**.

1. **Decisions.** S6-Q1 (Kontrol parent must be real, same patient, examined, not cancelled/deleted,
   server-derived) and S6-Q2 (no NO_CHARGE for a lab line) — `OWNER_POLICY_APPROVED`. S6-Q3 —
   `OWNER_POLICY_REVISED_AND_APPROVED`: a Kontrol may be Rp0; an additional treatment that is normally paid
   is billed at a **positive** price and paid normally; a mixed Rp0 + paid invoice is never NO_CHARGE.
   S6-Q3a: the approved free services are the `consultation` category (any visit) and the reserved
   `control` category (the Kontrol service — on a VALID Kontrol only; no master-data treatment uses it yet,
   production records the Kontrol service as Konsultasi Dokter). S6-Q3b: the issuance guard applies to
   Kontrol visits only and follows the flag. **The S6-Q3 revision SUPERSEDES the earlier "creator ≠ closer"
   recommendation (S6-Q3 open option)**: eligibility, not a second account, is the control; S6-D3 (the branch
   cashier closes, no second approval) is preserved.
2. **Eligibility.** `RmeZeroValueEligibility::isApprovedFreeTreatment()` is the single answer, used by the
   closure and by the issuance guard. Decided from the treatment identity and its master-data category —
   never a description; a free-text line is never free; the Kontrol link alone never makes anything free.
   A paid line makes the total positive (`ZERO_VALUE_TOTAL_NOT_ZERO`); a normally paid treatment at Rp0 is
   `ZERO_VALUE_CATEGORY_NOT_ELIGIBLE`; a lab line `ZERO_VALUE_LAB_LINE_EXCLUDED`; a discount to zero stays
   `ZERO_VALUE_LINE_NOT_FREE` (D21c unchanged). No new refusal code. Super Admin and any other account
   receive the same answer.
3. **Issuance guard (S6-Q3b).** `RmeInvoiceService::create()` — after server pricing, before an invoice
   number is drawn — refuses (`items`, message carries the stable code) on a server-derived Kontrol every line
   whose **net** value is Rp0 (priced at Rp0 **or discounted down to it**) that the closure would not accept,
   decided by the SAME per-line predicate `RmeZeroValueEligibility::lineRefusalCode()` (discount, voucher, lab,
   category); and any net-Rp0 line on a Kontrol whose parent is not valid (S6-Q1) — otherwise the invoice could be
   neither paid (amount > 0) nor closed. A line with a positive net value is billed and paid normally. **Flag-gated**: with `rme.zero_value_closure` OFF issuance is exactly
   production today. Non-Kontrol Rp0 issuance stays D21g, PENDING. D21 manual pricing is unchanged: no tariff
   is required; a paid treatment's price is whatever the authorized cashier types, but it must be > Rp0.
4. **Batch residual (#36 pattern) resolved.** `completeControlVisitIfSettled()` and
   `completeVisitAfterCashierBatch()` no longer complete a visit whose OWN invoice is an UNPAID Rp0 invoice the
   closure can close: the visit stays `cashier_pending` and the cashier presses "Selesai Tanpa Biaya". The
   parent payment is unchanged and attributed only to the parent; nothing marks the current invoice PAID or
   NO_CHARGE. An ineligible Rp0 invoice keeps the existing completion (only the closable case is held);
   flag OFF changes nothing. The payment page tells the cashier the next step. Historical invoices (#36,
   #42, #43) are not backfilled.
5. **Oversight (read-only).** `GET oversight/billing-corrections/zero-value-closures`
   (`oversight.billing-corrections.zero-value-closures.index`), the billing-correction oversight area: same
   gate (`clinic-oversight.view-billing-corrections`), permission (`view_billing_correction_oversight`) and
   branch scope (`ClinicOversightScope`, a filter only narrows). Filters: branch, period (WITA), category,
   treatment, doctor, closing cashier, invoice creator, invoice/visit reference (exact). Totals, per
   branch / cashier / doctor / treatment, and anomalies (same account issued and closed — informational,
   allowed by S6-D3; a NO_CHARGE invoice with a payment row — must be 0). No patient identity, no export,
   no mutation, no new permission.
6. **Mistakes.** NO_CHARGE stays terminal; there is no reversal. The incident procedure is in the SOP
   (`docs/operations/rme-rp0-selesai-tanpa-biaya-sop.md` §"Jika terjadi kesalahan"); recovery needs a separate
   owner decision. Never edit a NO_CHARGE invoice by SQL as an ordinary fix.
7. **Status.** `TECHNICAL_ENFORCEMENT_DEPLOYED` — runtime `ba33f9bb` (tree `2d1b684b`, PR #576), deployed 2026-11-01 04:34 UTC (12:34 WITA), production-verified, tag `hardening-rme-rp0-closure-owner-decisions-and-paid-treatment-1-go`. The flag
   stays OFF until `ACTIVATION-RME-RP0-CONTROL-CONSULTATION-1`.
8. **Rollback after activation (independent review LOW).** A visit held at `cashier_pending` by §9.4 becomes
   unreachable if the flag is switched OFF (the closure button disappears and a Rp0 invoice cannot be paid), and
   also if its parent is later soft-deleted or master data changes the line's category / `requires_lab`. Before
   switching the flag OFF, find the `cashier_pending` visits whose invoice is Rp0 on the cashier handoff board
   and close them "Selesai Tanpa Biaya" first. Never complete such a visit by SQL.
9. **Correction path.** A pre-payment correction cannot add a Rp0 line, and a corrected invoice is refused by
   the closure (`INVOICE_CORRECTED`), so corrections never reach `NO_CHARGE`.

## 10. Doctor declaration "Tidak Ada Tindakan" (rule 219, DPT-Q1) — operational KONTROL is NOT NO_CHARGE

Since `FEATURE-RME-DOCTOR-PERFORMED-TREATMENTS-1` the treating doctor can declare "Tidak Ada Tindakan"; that
classifies the visit as **operational KONTROL** (`RmeOperationalVisitCategory::CONTROL`). It changes nothing in
this rule:

- `OPERATIONAL_CONTROL != AUTOMATIC_NO_CHARGE`. `RmeZeroValueEligibility` never reads the doctor record; a
  Kontrol `NO_CHARGE` still needs a registered `visit_type = control` with a REAL examined parent of the same
  patient (S6-Q1) and approved free lines (S6-Q3).
- The declaration never rewrites `visit_type`, never creates or infers a parent visit, never zeroes an invoice.
- A parentless visit declared "Tidak Ada Tindakan" can only close Rp0 as a Konsultasi on its own merits.
- An empty treatment list is `NOT_RECORDED`, never a declaration.
- The doctor record reaches closures only as rule 218 evidence (detective, snapshot v2).
